content:
maya: Heads up — I opened a docs PR that reorganizes function/tool calling snippets and consolidates the structured-output JSON schema examples. Also moving SDK-specific snippets into /examples/sdk so they’re easier to sync. Need a quick QA pass before merge. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/482

sam: On it. Is this the one that changes the example shapes for tool responses? I'm worried about breaking references in other pages.

maya: Yes — the shape changes are small (make `result` required, add `metadata` optional). I added a migration note and a shim snippet showing client-side fallback. See the schema quickly inline: ```json
{"type":"object","properties":{"result":{"type":"object"},"metadata":{"type":"object"}},"required":["result"]}```

docs-ci-bot: CI: docs build succeeded — 3/3 checks passed :white_check_mark:

elaine: Quick question — the SDK snippet currently uses `SDK.v2.callTool(...)` which we don't ship yet. Can we change it to the generic `client.callTool`? @henry any objection?

henry: Agree with switching to `client.callTool`. Also we should rename the example file to `sdk-call-tool-compat.md` so search finds it. I'll push a tiny commit for the filename and the API change.

alex: I ran the new examples through our parser unit tests — one nit: the sample JSON uses snake_case keys but our canonical examples use camelCase. Can we standardize to camelCase?

maya: Good catch. I'll update the snippet to camelCase and add a line in the migration guide: "Expect keys to be camelCase in SDK examples."

sam: Also add a short section on graceful degradation: show code that catches missing `metadata` and proceeds. For example: ```js
try {
  const r = await client.callTool(...);
  const meta = r.metadata || {};
  // continue
} catch (e) {
  // fallback path
}
```

maya: Added that in the last commit. PTAL @sam @elaine — if no objections I'll merge tomorrow morning and cherry-pick to the release branch.

prs-bot: PR #482 labeled "docs: toolcall & structured output: snippet reorg" and assigned reviewers: sam, elaine

elaine: :thumbsup: LGTM — tiny wording nit but not blocking. Sam you good with merge?

sam: LGTM once it uses camelCase. Approving now.

maya: Thanks — merging after 24h unless any last comments. I'll open a short follow-up issue to track runtime compatibility feedback from SDK users.
